  {journeyIds:['LJ-12'],testId:'package-center-journey',scope:'Shipped UI and real Chromium/OPFS: image-caption-only two-tab conflicts preserve drafts and show actual current media; explicit acceptance retries an already committed Meaning after a failed Scene link without duplicates. Exact Scene read failure blocks dependent actions, while an unrelated annotation-list failure does not hide it. World Context replacement and later Scene acceptance preserve both user contexts in one Meaning. An actual persistent profile close/reopen retains separately saved Scene and accepted World revisions. A separate synthetic 10k unrelated-Meaning/text-only/loopback/1x-CPU case guards first acceptance and explicit update at 1.5s after visiting World, without complete command-frame reads. No paid providers, heavy-media or production capacity equivalence.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-12'],testId:'library-cloud',scope:'Actual Chromium/OPFS, Hono and disposable PostgreSQL: two devices restore the same unaccepted text/image Scene and real reveal pin, then independently accept different offline revisions into one stable Meaning identity. A current remote choice restores its exact facts while retaining immutable receipts; the discarded branch receipt cannot claim a nonexistent Anchor. A fresh explicit intent confirms the selected Scene without rewriting Meaning facts. A separate account deliberately reuses fixed command IDs: an untouched Scene held behind a note fork remains explicitly accept-able after selecting the local note, retaining both independent first acceptance and later updates. Scene, original learning facts and backup admission survive reload. Synthetic low-media published Targets; not all offline interleavings or real provider/audio quality.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-12'],testId:'learning-scene-bridge',scope:'A controlled in-memory Journey repository accepts supplied published semantic facts, preserves exact Sense/Expression/Binding identities, replays an exact receipt and updates the same Meaning/Anchor only after a new explicit scene acceptance. This is a module-contract fixture, not real Book admission, OPFS, media decoding, UI or Cloud transport.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-12'],testId:'personal-learning-scene',scope:'Actual Book admission, enrollment and initial Run over SQLite/Wasm: scene edit bases reject stale drafts without receipts; explicit reviewed replacement retains identity/history. Failed commits roll back, lost-response replay cannot overwrite a later scene, and a failed annotation-list read does not deny a durable save. Real reveal/rating actions pin their respective immutable scene revisions; the complete snapshot passes backup validation. One synthetic low-media target, no paid provider, not Chromium, Cloud or capacity proof.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'personal-meaning-correction',scope:'Actual manual acceptance and scoped SQLite/Wasm correction replace one current connection in the same Meaning, preserve original Context/acceptance/Alignment snapshots, and reject stale Context, failed commits and changed exact retries. Old unchanged replicas cannot re-activate the retired interpretation; missing correction witnesses reject backup/merge. Current Context composition is explicitly read before correction, previous capture stays historical. Small deterministic owner command/read/replica tests, not UI, Chromium, media capacity or whole-journey completion.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'personal-learning',scope:'Actual personal preparation with controlled model/speech, saved ContentAttempts, Targets and Memory/Run history: correcting the original Meaning leaves every nonsemantic owner table unchanged, removes only its current source from selection, and the complete backup validates historical fixed source/Context pins. Memory Library/HTTP fixtures and real domain commands, not paid providers, Chromium/OPFS transport or scale.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'scene-editor-read',scope:'Real React editor with controlled exact Context reads: initial loading/read failure disable text/images/save, retry reads original content, and a keyed target switch ignores the previous response before saving only the new Context. Happy DOM and a presentation-only overlay stand-in; not Chromium focus/layout, OPFS persistence, scene CAS or draft durability.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'learner-library-projection',scope:'Actual nonbundled Portable admission, explicit enrollment, favorite/note, reveal/rating and mastery over SQLite/Wasm drive canonical Target references without auto-World or invented learning. Annotation read failure/retry stays unknown until ready; controlled DTOs preserve separate Target IDs sharing one Sense. A separate synthetic 10k raw-clone projection stress checks compact list bytes, zero source hydration, selected-only detail, cache rebuild and source/metadata rollback. That stress is not a validated 10k learner collection, OPFS/browser latency or whole-journey capacity proof.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'world-browse-storage',scope:'Actual Meaning acceptance/clarification/delete commands supply two sources; a controlled read fixture removes the deleted source binding confirmations to exercise historical unbound trash. Memory and SQLite/Wasm reads agree across filters/search, while continuation remains based on the different active unfinished Meaning. Small read-adapter parity, not a public incomplete-Meaning creation path, UI or cross-device transport.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-11'],testId:'personal-meaning-lifecycle',scope:'Actual manual Semantic Intake acceptance and gateway operations over SQLite/Wasm: bounded delete/restore, original facts/history, failed-commit rollback, exact replay, stale edits and tombstone material-write rejection. Indexed trash, read-only detail and exact Sense references exclude or restore the same identity. Replica admission rejects missing/mismatched lifecycle receipts. A real installed/enrolled lightweight target, started Run, accepted personal scene and reveal/rate outcome survive delete/restore unchanged; both complete snapshots pass backup validation. No Chromium, cross-device transport, comprehensive conflict or capacity claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'study-scope-storage',scope:"Actual 64-member Book admission retains all 64 Targets while a one-participant Run records only its selected immutable source. An isolated SQLite/Wasm kernel stores those exact Scope bytes, preserves exact membership and rolls back an interrupted owner write; an existing corrupt body rejects without replacement. Separate raw typed representation data with 130 distinct bodies verifies a second ownership-batch failure rolls back the first 128 owners and all body rows. That representation fixture is not an accepted product operation or learning outcome. Controlled low-media facts/storage faults, not a dependency-complete product restore, Chromium latency, real providers or whole-journey completion."},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'package-center-journey',scope:'Production-build UI with a synthetic 100-member Book and real OPFS repeats pause, preference changes, reload and exact revealed-Step resume twelve times in each isolated and persistent Chromium context. Verifies unchanged Session/Scope, Run/material pins, zero learning outcomes, original Portable export bytes and full integrity. The persistent first preference change includes explicitly measured idle with no scripted SQL, navigation or CLI restore during the wait; default two seconds cannot claim long idle. Bounded lifecycle/explicit-duration regression, not HMR, 10k admitted capacity or a root-cause explanation of independent UAT storage faults.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'personal-learning',scope:'An actual accepted Personal Meaning intent can be withdrawn before preparation, with zero model calls or fabricated Target. Explicit restore preserves its Task. Controlled generator/speech preparation then revises support language within the same Route, admits material and starts a new Scope while retaining its earlier active membership decision snapshot; full domain validation passes. No paid providers, Chromium UI or capacity claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'direct-learning-provisioning',scope:'Controlled model transport holds the real on-demand preparation callback while the public Learning command withdraws its direct intent. The late response cannot submit a ready Target or initiate review; subsequent preparation rejects before another provider request. Explicit restore reuses the Task and admits exactly one Target. Actual Content Supply/Learning interfaces with synthetic providers, not paid services, UI, OPFS or cross-device conflict evidence.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'supplemental-membership',scope:'Actual accepted direct intents and Portable Book admissions over SQLite/Wasm remove and restore pending or ready Supplemental sources with revision checks and idempotent receipts. Withdrawal blocks preparation before Target creation, removes future candidates without rewriting an active Scope/Run, and preserves the shared Target/history under overlapping Book coverage. Explicit restoration resumes the original Run with a new Scope decision snapshot. A real derived-index write interruption rolls source/index/receipt back together; competing stale revisions settle once. Bounded management pages cover 64 actual accepted intents without complete source-table enumeration, duplicates or Route-crossing cursors. Full backup validation rejects a foreign Target reference. Controlled storage, not public UI, OPFS lifecycle, cross-device transport or 10k latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'learning-session-end',scope:'Actual Book admission and public Learning commands over SQLite/Wasm end an unfinished activity without Target, material, Action, Memory or Introduction changes. Stale/future/backdated inputs reject; a real adapter commit fault rolls back all facts, exact end replay is idempotent, and cacheless validation rejects forged end/pause witnesses or a false completion. A later start uses the updated quantity and fixed ordinal Range while pairing the original Run pause/resume and preserving origin Scope/material; real completion later leaves that earlier end witness valid. Competing end/Action commands settle only one reviewed revision. Controlled storage/clock, not Chromium/OPFS, complete multi-device conflicts or capacity.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'learning-reconciliation',scope:'Controlled independent Book enrollment records on one Route are merged through the actual replica module. The two active sources become explicit cross-record conflicts, and partitioning preserves each side instead of silently selecting or rewriting a Book. A metadata-only legacy full-Scope fixture locks actual active-Run participant policy but not an unstarted future Target. Minimal synthetic records test the merge boundary, not full domain admission, OPFS, Cloud transport, conflict-resolution UI or comprehensive multi-device behavior.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'learning-session-scope',scope:"Actual Book admission and Learning commands over SQLite/Wasm record only selected Run participants without Target, Scope, Enrollment or removal-table enumeration. An unrelated corrupt material does not prevent a healthy selection. Default20 and first Run/Session commit atomically; a failed commit preserves all prior facts. Pausing the original Book, narrowing its ordinal range and adding another Book leave current work unchanged, while the next Run selects the newly eligible source in the same Session with its original quota. Each Run has its own source snapshot; the Session origin stays unchanged. Quantity changes affect a later activity. Committed Policy edits reject; unsupported unstarted methods still fail the real resource gate. Full/cacheless restore validation rejects forged source-policy snapshots. Common purpose-readiness guards remain independent. Controlled storage, not UI, OPFS or complete multi-device conflict resolution."},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'learning-runtime-query',scope:'Public Home and workspace queries use the same exact language pair after an in-place Route support-language revision. Actual Portable admissions under a controlled Library adapter exclude old-pair future candidates, preserve the open Run and its original pinned pair, and include a newly accepted current-pair Target. No OPFS timing, UI support editor, full Session Scope or capacity claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'library-cloud',scope:'Real Chromium/OPFS and disposable PostgreSQL transport actual Learning histories with Scope/Session facts through checkpoint and restore. An explicitly ended unfinished activity restores and reloads with its original Step/Scope/Introduction, no active pointers, no completion/Memory and no public package bytes. Server rejects individually omitting previously published Scope, Session or Run rows while allowing ordinary lifecycle updates and lossless repacking. Controlled authentication, not Book Plan controls, comprehensive active-Scope policy-conflict resolution, account UI, production latency or capacity.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'book-plan-planning',scope:'Actual admitted Book bytes supply fixed Manifest ordinal/Sense selection; invalid/omitted ordinals reject, unchanged Range survives factory mode changes, and mode-only index updates avoid range writes while reused Range IDs with changed contents cannot retain stale rows. Synthetic SQLite/Wasm phase/readiness inputs exercise precise package×Sense×Binding selection, maintenance, pause, alternate coverage, newer blocked-source fallback and Target deduplication against the pure oracle. Separate actual overlapping Book admission and public change_book_plan commands maintain the old active Book, reactivate the reviewed Book with a fixed ordinal Range and pause the alternate; Learning start binds the eligible old source. Range-excluded start rejects without switching the Run, and prepare_queue adds no outside Targets. Explicit direct selection admits its own source for the excluded Target, preserving the Run until a separate start. Controlled storage, not UI, genuine completion/Memory outcomes, OPFS latency or capacity.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'book-curriculum-sources',scope:'Actual overlapping Book archives and public Learning commands over SQLite/Wasm retain independent source-bound admissions for one Target/Retention identity. Adding/repeating Book B preserves the revealed Run and Book A membership; both Book upgrades reuse identical Package bytes without refreshing their old paused/active Run materials. Cacheless domain validation rejects a self-consistent new A-only member falsely attributed to B, a correctly rehashed new Run material naming a foreign Book version, and source Ready time drift inside a genuinely re-applied membership update window. No assertion about rewriting older source-unbound witnesses, mode/Range/Scope UI, paid provider, OPFS, Cloud transport or scale.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'book-publication-provenance',scope:'Actually admitted Books share the same Portable bytes in different Manifest orders. SQLite/Wasm facts retain exact positions without duplicate Packages. Partial recovery, only-missing-source retry, warm no-download recovery, lost cache position repair and concurrent genuine source admission with its disposable publication removed never falsely report complete. Explicit non-primary Book enrollment passes cacheless backup domain validation; forged Book/duplicate positions reject. Final SQLite write failure rolls back facts and both projections. Controlled cacheless-concurrency setup, not Cloud transport, Learning outcomes, Range/mode UI, OPFS latency, authored learning-order or publisher trust.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'package-center-journey',scope:'Shipped Chromium/OPFS UI installs two Books sharing Portable members; cache recovery restores exact Manifest positions without enrolling. Independent admissions and explicit upgrade retain revealed source/material identities. Future mode/ordinal editing retains the entire old Scope through failed writes, missing responses, confirmed-save read failure, reload and continuation; switching the active Book maintains the old one, and explicit reactivation preserves the current Run. Quantity changes retain old Scope/quota through successor and completed-session finish. Explicit unfinished-activity end preserves its Step through faults and offline reload, with a new Scope/quota only on explicit start; stale two-tab confirmation cannot end a successor. 320px controls remain reachable. No all-protocol, authored learning-order, capacity, Cloud conflict resolution or external publisher-trust claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'package-learning',scope:'Actual admitted Portable targets and public Learning commands: a declaration interrupts planning, revocation preserves another active Run and produces no grade/Memory update; only explicit selection resumes the original revealed Run/material. Controlled clock/storage, not Web/OPFS, automatic-completion, quota capacity or Book Range delivery.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-10'],testId:'local-i18n',scope:'The existing 15-locale resource contract also checks translation of the explicit missing-operation-receipt notice. Does not prove save/rollback, OPFS or UI recovery.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-09'],testId:'relearning-loop',scope:'Actual Initial and due Again Review commands over SQLite/Wasm, then repeated Relearning failure: write fault rollback, exact command replay before/after completion, noncompletion history, explicit same-target continuation and cacheless authority replay. A stale explicit repair retry cannot start a later due Review. Preserves review-only intent, original Memory Outcome and FSRS schedule; no browser, provider or capacity claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08','LJ-16'],testId:'library-sync-transport',scope:'Public sync interface with SQLite/Wasm and controlled malformed transport rejects an unrequested missing hash without head-race retry or learner-fact mutation. An unversioned confirmed baseline cannot skip the current manifest format gate; incompatible data remains untouched with a terminal failure. No HTTP, OPFS, provider, capacity or heap claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08','LJ-16'],testId:'library-sync-blocks',scope:'Lossless deterministic transport encoding reuses immutable body segments without merging row identities or clocks. UTF-8 chunk boundaries preserve surrogate pairs; corrupt digests, invalid base64, forged inflation sizes and truncated-prefix attacks reject. Pure codec evidence, not real cloud, browser latency, capacity or history replay.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08','LJ-10','LJ-16'],testId:'shared-learning-storage',scope:'Actual Initial and due Review commands over SQLite/Wasm share immutable content across Target/Run snapshots without merging their identities or times. Failed compatible admission rolls back source, indexes, receipts and content owners together; sync baseline owns exact bodies through local clearing. Corrupt body reads fail closed. Framed shared/gzip backup rejects missing/corrupt/orphan/duplicate/truncated frames before writes and encrypted empty-destination restore preserves genuine cacheless history. Genuine v14 table-name constraints upgrade atomically for records, tombstones and sync baseline, preserving encoded bytes, rowids, indexes and body ownership; interruption during the third table rebuild rolls all changes back, then retry admits Scope/Session baseline and tombstone writes. Genuine clustered v16/v17 baseline layouts upgrade with exact source/base/body/owner/tombstone bytes and explicit indexes; copy, swap and header failures roll back before retry, and duplicate/NULL keys remain rejected. Synthetic low media and controlled storage; not OPFS latency, large capacity, audio quality or Cloud transfer normalization.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'local-learning-runtime',scope:'Controlled formal Protocol fixtures retain distinct Initial Completion, due Review and Relearning authority. Genuine cacheless Structured backups still check exact rehashed Run material source admission and presentation times; moving Ready before source admission/after Run start, or moving a refreshed snapshot/source after its actual presentation event rejects. Does not establish complete Structured replay without its resources or a shipped Structured user entry; that capability remains outside current Web acceptance.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'personal-learning',scope:'Real personal preparation through controlled model/speech adapters records the Content Attempt actual Ready instant and transfers it unchanged to admitted material. Backdated Run creation rejects with all source, Target, Run, active-selection and receipt tables unchanged; actual private-to-published material refresh history remains restorable without package cache. No paid providers, shipped UI or capacity claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-target-view',scope:'Real React Target-view hook with controlled read results: B can explicitly retry while an initial A read remains pending, A late response cannot overwrite B, and returning to A requests the new view. No prepare/rehydrate/content workspace commands. No learning facts seeded; not Chromium/OPFS or latency evidence.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-runtime-query',scope:'Public Runtime and Target-detail projections match the complete workspace presentation while rejecting collection/history enumeration. Current source summaries use exact keys over the actual SQLite/Wasm kernel with full Package and media hydration forbidden. Detail requires the current pinned language pair, exact Target/active Run reads and exact export-key presence; errors reject rather than report a missing Target. Controlled Node storage, not OPFS/UI latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-history-page',scope:'30k synthetic scalar history projections exercise public paged history counts, cursor ordering, languages, calendar filters, invalid/future ranges and DST in SQLite/Wasm against complete-record selection. Summary groups remain language-specific; only bounded record JSON is decoded, not Target/Run/Event facts. Projection shape/parity, not manufactured learning outcomes, browser timezone or OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08','LJ-10'],testId:'runtime-learning-candidates',scope:'SQLite/Wasm scalar scheduling index matches the complete pure queue on 10k synthetic projection inputs, including current/Retry exclusions, policy readiness, pinned language pair, daily quota and next-change timing. Rejected candidates refill a new-learning prefix at quota1 in both adapters without consuming quota. Worker result is bounded to candidate prefixes plus exact retries; no Target/material JSON decode in the index query or unchanged index open. Projection shape/parity, not genuine learning history or OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-command-receipt',scope:'Production Learning commands persist bounded receipts rather than duplicate Run/material payloads. Exact original metadata replays after later progress without resubmission; altered input conflicts. Restore and live replay reject a receipt pointing at another genuine Run for the same Target or a changed context/intent/time. Controlled storage, not Chromium/OPFS latency.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-material-pins',scope:'Formal actions at different instants share exact immutable bodies. Actual v1/v2/v3 unacted refreshes and same-instant Again/reveal/completion replay by continuous Action/lifecycle Run revisions without public cache or device receipts. Saved protocol Steps cite acted material, first-binding order survives sorted encoding, and missing/duplicate/gapped causal witnesses, reordered refreshes, future next material and unreferenced bodies reject. A start before actual local source admission rejects without writes; correctly rehashed pins cannot erase Ready or move it before admission/after Run start. Controlled storage; no capacity, external publisher trust or latency verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'learning-management-query',scope:'Actual initial completion, Again Review and Relearning over SQLite/Wasm produce compact Study records identical to the full projection without hydrating Target/Run/Event payloads. Unfinished initial Again has no completion record; a formal failed Review remains a Review attempt. An index write failure rolls back facts and receipts. Missing local tables/indexes rebuild from unchanged facts and read errors fail closed. Not an OPFS/UI latency claim.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08','LJ-10'],testId:'retention-review-capacity',scope:"Specialized isolated Chromium/OPFS baseline with actual Initial Completion and due Review history generated through LearningSystem commands over SQLite/Wasm, fully replay-validated by the Node producer before digest-checked bounded fixture copying. Explicit Target-detail review start verifies the actual bounded selection and persisted Session before reveal/rating-to-next; stored Target count remains complete and successor Run has its own selected scope. First activity creation and continuation costs are distinct. Measures UI Study/statistics/history/reload separately from setup cost; read failures hide stale facts and explicit retry restores actual records. Pagination/type filters retain full-range counts. Copying is not product backup restore. Configurable count, synthetic low-media source, 1x CPU; registration is not a passing capacity or audio-quality verdict."},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'library-transaction-and-replay',scope:'Actual SQLite/Wasm kernel in Node: supplied crossday clock selects superseded introductions through indexed date ranges and active due targets through Route indexes. Synthetic 10k already-retained compact scheduling rows (5k due) exercise Home planning with a 1500ms regression ceiling, no materials/history returned. Zero history Runs: not Chromium/OPFS latency, genuine completion history, review settlement or a full user-performance verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'review-session',scope:'Production Learning interface with actual Portable admission and a controlled Library adapter: review-only selects genuine due work instead of a paused initial Run, persists its intent across continuation, preserves the original Step, and finishes before new learning. Hard/Again remain canonical grades; exact replay and stale revision protect one Review settlement, distinct Relearning does not reschedule again. Backup validation without public artifact cache replays lightweight history and rejects altered memory revisions/grades. Future command timestamps and review-only initial work reject without writes; explicit three-member Book enrollment and quantity change create no initial eligibility during review-only. Adapter contract rejects intent/language mutation. Not shipped UI, OPFS latency, long-history capacity or external-provider evidence.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-08'],testId:'package-center-journey',scope:'Shipped Chromium/OPFS UI with a compiled two-member Book: actual first-learning nextReviewAt defines a browser-clock-only crossday simulation; review-only switches away from a paused revealed initial Step. Failed rating write, two-tab Hard settlement, offline reload, lost Again receipt and separate Relearning/reload retain exactly-once outcomes and the original initial Step. Genuine near-midnight completion uses the actual Worker local calendar. A deliberately blocked Statistics code module offers effective reload after reconnect without changing saved records. No seeded learning schedules, paid provider or whole capacity verdict.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-07','LJ-10'],testId:'learning-runtime-query',scope:'Production Learning interface with admitted Portable fixtures and a controlled Library adapter: exact current Run/participant reads, no collection planning during a Step, no material/history enumeration; continuation planning only at a Run boundary. A ready due review does not inspect unrelated initial content. Home uses existing indexed counts and exact choices without all-Target hydration, including current support-language changes while preserving the open Run. Same-operation reveal/Again replay and stale revision rejection, no initial completion or FSRS before hard/good. Controlled read shape and settlement, not OPFS latency or long-history capacity.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-07'],testId:'learning-question',scope:'Read-only optional teaching with a controlled model port: current reveal scope before/after response, bounded adopted textual facts, no media disclosure, pre-reveal/stopped/late response rejection, unchanged Learning workspace. Private-derived resources and extra scene text require a separate current-teacher opt-in, not a Content Attempt grant; a changed recipient rejects before the model. No real provider, browser dialog or audible evidence.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-07'],testId:'operation-settlement',scope:'A missing command response triggers a read without resubmission or claiming commit; failed recovery reads retain uncertainty. Known durable success is separate from refresh failure. Pure settlement logic, not actual OPFS failure.'},
  {journeyIds:['LJ-07'],testId:'model-disclosure-preflight',scope:'Production client transport with controlled queue/account adapters: teacher assignment and account changes while queued reject before fetch at dispatch. No network, actual provider or complete account-transition UI claim.'},
